# Custom Colorscale for Contour Plot

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

A custom colour scale is a list of `[stop, color]` pairs where `stop` is a float 0–1
and `color` is a CSS string. Stops must be in ascending order starting at 0 and ending at 1.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Contour}

z = for i <- 0..19 do
  for j <- 0..19 do
    :math.sin(i * :math.pi() / 10) * :math.cos(j * :math.pi() / 10)
  end
end

custom_scale = [
  [0.0, "rgb(166,206,227)"],
  [0.25, "rgb(31,120,180)"],
  [0.45, "rgb(178,223,138)"],
  [0.65, "rgb(51,160,44)"],
  [0.85, "rgb(251,154,153)"],
  [1.0, "rgb(227,26,28)"]
]

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(
  Contour.new(
    z: z,
    colorscale: custom_scale,
    contours: %{showlabels: true, labelfont: %{color: "black", size: 10}}
  )
)
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Contour with Custom Colourscale")
|> Plotly.show()
```
